From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FE Fates port <engine@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:08:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: hear the New Game step

Round 81b (docs/ROUND81B_PLAN.md D1-D4; the owner's "fix the classic bug
first", Grok's call in docs/collab/ROUND81B_CLASSIC_GROK.md). The
randomizer's NewGameWatch only sees a New Game when GameConfigData word +0x4
changes, and on Normal + Classic it does not (docs/RANDOMIZER_INGAME.md
section 16): no pick, no randomized run, no Nuzlocke, no message. Now the
randomizer also hears round 81's StartFromBeginning trap (patch 0040).

- D1 (fates_options.rs): the trap word (svc 0xEFFEC003 over 0x001D0618,
  original 0xE92D4070) is wanted while a New Game row is set OR the
  randomizer listens (trap_wanted; fates_rando_session::hears_step =
  listens: the Fates title id, Config::fates_rando, and the game Fates
  itself, step_game). Seal of Flames keeps the hooks on (F-047) but does not
  listen: Seal at the defaults lays no trap, hears nothing and shows no
  warning, as in round 81 (plan D1, P7). The rest as round 81: a stranger
  word left alone, checks_itself() false = off, a state put right. Not
  listening and no row: no trap and no guest memory read.
- D2 (fates_options::on_svc, svc_outcome): the same checks, run once (ARM at
  0x001D0618, lr 0x00441794, r0 == *0x006DA0F8 non-zero, block readable, no
  player army, no map). Held: the rows' pending store only while a row is
  set (exactly round 81), and "the New Game step heard" for the randomizer
  (fates_rando_session::heard_step) while it listens, stamped with the
  frame whose end takes it. Refused: round 81's log line while a row is set,
  else a randomizer log line; the refusal goes to the randomizer too. No
  guest data byte written in the svc.
- D3 (fates_rando_session.rs): Session::frame_heard: a pick is NewGameWatch
  fired OR the step heard in this frame; at most one pick per frame; a pick
  within SAME_PICK = 2 frames after a pick is the same New Game; the
  save-read load window still means no pick. take_heard clears the flag at
  the frame's end and drops one stamped for another frame (a jump); a state
  restore drops it and the SAME_PICK count. Session::frame(g) = frame_heard(g, false, false), so the
  watch-only path is as before.
- D4: while the randomizer listens, once each per program run, on screen (the notice)
  and in the log: the step refused (or heard inside the load window) and no
  pick taken that frame -> "This New Game did not use your seed."; the trap
  cannot be laid (a stranger word, or recompiled code that cannot check
  itself; Writer::cannot_lay keeps round 81's single rows line apart) ->
  "Classic New Games cannot start the randomizer in this setup; pick Casual
  or Phoenix."

Unchanged: the randomizer's output (answer, run id, patch), the page, round
81's rows and bytes, loads (a load never reaches the step: lr check).

Tests: fates_options the_trap_is_wanted_for_the_rows_or_the_randomizer,
hooks_off_and_no_rows_lay_no_trap_and_touch_no_guest_memory,
the_randomizer_alone_lays_the_trap_and_the_rows_store_stays_empty,
rows_and_randomizer_share_one_check,
a_trap_that_cannot_be_laid_is_said_once_to_each_listener;
fates_rando_session a_classic_new_game_is_heard_at_the_trap_once,
a_casual_new_game_heard_and_watched_in_one_frame_is_one_pick,
a_watch_after_a_heard_pick_is_the_same_new_game,
a_load_is_no_pick_and_is_never_heard,
the_heard_flag_lives_for_its_own_frame_only,
a_refusal_is_said_once_and_takes_no_pick,
only_fates_itself_hears_the_new_game_step. Round 81's tests unchanged and
passing. Fourteen code mutations each fail at least one test
(build/r81b/core/planted.txt), and two more for the Seal gate and the
restore (build/r81b/gate/planted-gate.txt). zakuro-core 271 passed in
engine/target/zakuro-core-test, zakuro 131 passed (2 ignored) in
engine/target/zakuro-frontend-test.

