+//!
+//! **Round 81b (docs/ROUND81B_PLAN.md D1-D4): the randomizer hears the same step.** The
+//! randomizer's `NewGameWatch` only sees a New Game when word +0x4 changes, and on Normal +
+//! Classic it does not (docs/RANDOMIZER_INGAME.md section 16). So the trap is also laid while
+//! the randomizer listens (`fates_rando_session::hears_step`: the Fates title id,
+//! `Config::fates_rando`, and the game is Fates itself, not Seal of Flames: the port's frontend
+//! keeps the hooks on for Seal too, F-047, but Seal at the defaults stays as in round 81, no
+//! trap), even with every row at Game's choice. At the
+//! svc the same checks run once: when they hold, "the New Game step was heard" goes to the
+//! randomizer for this frame (`fates_rando_session::heard_step`) whatever the rows; the rows'
+//! pending store is recorded only while a row is set, exactly as before. A refusal, or a trap
+//! that cannot be laid (a stranger word, recompiled code that cannot check itself), is said to
+//! the player once by the randomizer's notice. The randomizer not listening (`Config::fates_rando`
